hadiths[39]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1238","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he divorced his wife during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while she was menstruating. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about this, so he (ﷺ) said: ""Tell Ibn Umar to take his wife back, then keep her in his marriage until she becomes pure from her menstruation. Then she should menstruate again and then become pure. Then, if he wishes, he may keep his wife in marriage, and if he wishes, he may divorce her before having intercourse with her. This is the prescribed period of purity in which Allah has commanded the women to be divorced."""
"1239","Abu Zubair narrated that Abdur Rahman bin Aiman, the freed slave of Azza, was asking Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), and Abu Zubair was listening. He asked: ""What is your opinion about a man who divorces his wife while she is menstruating?"" Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) replied that Abdullah bin Umar (i.e., he himself) had divorced his wife during her menstruation, so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Tell him (Ibn Umar) to take his wife back, and when she becomes pure from her menstruation, then if he wishes, he may divorce her or keep her in marriage."" Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, Allah the Exalted has said: ""O Prophet! When you divorce women, divorce them at the commencement of their waiting period."" Imam Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) was uncertain in «في قُبل عدتهن» and «لقبل عدتهن» ."
"1240","It is narrated from Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) that he also used to recite «فطلقوهن لعدتهن» as «في قبل عدتهن» ."
"1241","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he used to recite in this manner: «اذا طلقتم النساء فطلقوهن لقبل عدتهن» ."
"1242","Abu Zubair narrated that he heard Abdullah bin Ayman asking Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), and Abu Zubair was listening: ""What is your opinion about a man who divorces his wife while she is menstruating?"" He replied that during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) divorced his wife while she was menstruating. When Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Tell Ibn Umar to take her back."" She was returned to me and it was not considered a problem, and he said: ""When she becomes pure from her menstruation, then if you wish, divorce her or keep her in marriage."""
"1243","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he divorced his wife during her menstruation in the time of the Prophet ﷺ. When Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Order Ibn Umar to take her back."" The Prophet ﷺ returned the woman to me without any objection, and said: ""When she becomes pure from her menstruation, then he may divorce her or keep her in his marriage."""
"1244","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he divorced his wife during her menstrual period in the time of the Prophet ﷺ. When Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Tell Ibn Umar to take her back, then keep her with him until she becomes pure from her menstruation, then she has her menses again, and when she becomes pure after that, if he wishes, he may keep her in his marriage, and if he wishes, he may divorce her before having intercourse with her in that period of purity. This is the waiting period in which Allah has commanded women to be divorced."""
"1245","It is narrated from Ibn Jurayj that he sent a man to Nafi‘ (may Allah have mercy on him) to ask whether, in the time of the Prophet ﷺ, the divorce given by Ibn ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was counted. He replied: ""Yes."""
"1246","It is narrated from Tawus that Abu As-Sahba asked Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), ""Were three divorces counted as only one during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), the caliphate of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and the first three years of the caliphate of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)?"" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) replied, ""Yes."""
"1247","Mujahid narrated that a man said to Ibn Abbas, ""I have pronounced divorce upon my wife a hundred times."" So he (Ibn Abbas) said: ""Take three and leave ninety-seven."""
"1248","Muhammad bin Iyas bin Bukair narrated that a man gave his wife three divorces before consummation, then he planned to marry her again, so he came to ask about the issue and inquired from Abu Hurairah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them). They said: In our opinion, he cannot marry her until she marries another husband. The man said, ""I intended only one divorce."" Ibn Abbas said: You have used up all your (entire) right."
"1249","Ata bin Sayyar (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that a man came and asked Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) about a man who gave his wife three divorces before consummation. Ata bin Sayyar (may Allah have mercy on him) says, I said, ""For a virgin, only one will apply."" So Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""You are a storyteller; one divorce will make her irrevocably separated, and three will make her unlawful for him until she marries another husband."""
"1250","Muhammad bin Iyas bin Bukair narrated that a man gave his wife three divorces before consummation of marriage. Later, when he intended to marry that woman again, he came to ask about the ruling, so I accompanied him to inquire about the matter for him. Then he asked Abu Hurairah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding this, so both of them said, ""In our opinion, he cannot marry her until she marries another husband."" The man said, ""I had only given her one divorce."" Upon this, Ibn Abbas said, ""You have used up all your right."" Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said that Abu Hurairah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) did not consider it objectionable that he gave three divorces."
"1251","It is narrated from Ata bin Yasar that a man came to Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) to ask about the case of a man who had given his wife three divorces before consummation of marriage. Ata says, I said, ""Indeed, in the case of a virgin, one (divorce) will be effective."" So Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""One divorce will make her irrevocably separated, and three will make her unlawful for him until she marries another husband."" Imam Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said that Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), when he was told that he had given three divorces, did not say, ""You have done very badly"" (i.e., he did not express anger at this action)."
"1252","It is narrated from Ibn Abi Ayash that he was sitting with Abdullah bin Zubair and Asim bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) when Muhammad bin Iyas bin Bukair came to them and asked: ""A man from among the desert dwellers has given his wife three divorces before consummating the marriage. What do you say about this?"" Upon this, Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""We do not have any knowledge about this matter. You should go to Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with them). I have found both of them present at Aisha's (may Allah be pleased with her) place. Ask them about the issue and then come back and inform us as well."" He went and asked them, so Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): ""He has brought a serious matter to you, so give him a verdict!"" Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""One divorce will make her irrevocably separated, and three will make her unlawful for him until she marries another husband."" And Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) also said the same. Imam Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ""These three companions and Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) did not dislike this."""
"1253","It is narrated from the noble wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), that the wife of Rifa’ah (al-Qurazi) came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Rifa’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) divorced me, and it was an irrevocable (final) divorce. Then ‘Abdur Rahman bin Zubair married me, but he has something like the edge of a garment (i.e., he is impotent). So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you wish to return to Rifa’ah? That is not permissible until you taste his (your current husband’s) sweetness and he tastes yours.”"
"1254","It is narrated from Zubair bin Abdur Rahman bin Zubair that Rifa’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) divorced his wife Tamimah bint Wahb three times during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then Abdur Rahman bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) married her, but he separated from her before consummating the marriage. So Rifa’ah (may Allah be pleased with him), who was her first husband and had divorced her, wanted to marry her again. This matter was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, so he forbade him from marrying her and said: “She is not lawful for you until she tastes the sweetness of marriage with her present husband.”"
"1255","It is narrated from the noble wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), that she said: The wife of Rifa’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) al-Qurazi came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""I was the wife of Rifa’ah and he gave me an irrevocable divorce. Then I married Abdur Rahman bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him), and with him, he is like the edge of a garment (i.e., he is impotent)."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled at this and said, ""Do you wish to return to Rifa’ah? This will not be permissible for you until you and your present husband have consummated the marriage."" Urwah said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and the Prophet ﷺ were sitting there, while Khalid bin Sa’id bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) was standing at the door, waiting for permission to enter. He called out, ""O Abu Bakr! Do you not hear what this woman is saying to the Prophet ﷺ?"""
"1256","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the wife of Rifa’ah Al-Qurazi came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “I was with Rifa’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) and he divorced me three times. Then after him, I married Abdur Rahman bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him), and with him, he is like the edge of a garment (i.e., he is impotent).” Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said: “Do you wish to return to Rifa’ah? This cannot happen until he tastes your sweetness and you taste his sweetness.” Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, while Khalid bin Sa’id bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) was standing at the door waiting for permission. He called out: “O Abu Bakr! Do you not hear what this woman is saying to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?”"
"1257","Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say that whoever gives his slave permission to marry, then the right of divorce belongs only to the slave; no one other than the slave has the right of divorce."
"1258","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Harith Al-Taimi (may Allah have mercy on him) that Nafi’, who had corresponded with Umm al-Mu’minin Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), asked Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) about an issue: “I have given two divorces to my free wife.” So Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “She has become unlawful for you.”"
"1259","It is narrated from Sulaiman bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that Nafi’, who had corresponded with Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), was married to a free woman. He gave her two divorces, then wanted to take her back, so the purified wives of the Prophet ﷺ told him to ask ‘Uthman bin ‘Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) about it. He went to him and found him at the place of Darj, and he was holding the hand of Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him). He asked both of them, and they immediately replied: “She has become unlawful for you, she has become unlawful for you.”"
"1260","It is narrated from Ibn Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that Nafi', who had corresponded with Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyidah Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), gave his free wife two divorces. Then he asked 'Uthman ibn 'Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) about the matter, so 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him that she has become unlawful for you."
"1261","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: ""In Khul‘ and Baryah as well, divorce takes place three times."""
"1262","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she stated: Three Sunnahs were established with Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her). One of them is that when she was set free, she was also given the choice regarding her husband (i.e., if she wished, she could maintain the marriage or annul it)."
"1263","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said regarding the slave woman who is married to a slave and her master sets her free: if her husband has not had intercourse with her, then she has a choice; but if he has had intercourse with her, then she has no choice."
"1264","It is narrated from Urwah bin Zubair (may Allah have mercy on him) that the freed slave woman of Banu Adi bin Ka'b, whose name was Zabra, informed him that she was married to a slave, and at that time she was a slave woman when her master set her free. She says that the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her), sent a message to her and called her, and said: ""I am going to tell you something, and I do not like that you should do anything (hasty). That is, your matter is now in your own hands until your husband has intercourse with you."" So she separated herself from her husband three times."
"1265","It is narrated from Urwah that the freed slave woman of Bani Adi, whose name was Zabra, informed him that when she was a slave, she was married to a slave man. Her master set her free. She says that Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) sent for me with a message and said: ""I am going to tell you something, and I do not want you to do anything (hasty), and that is: now your matter is in your own hands until your husband has intercourse with you."" She says that he separated from her three times. Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said that Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) did not say to her that it is not permissible for you to give him three divorces."
"1266","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when mention was made to him of the husband of Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her), he said: ""He was Mughith, the slave of such-and-such tribe. It is as if I can still see him, weeping and walking behind her along the road."""
"1267","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that Barirah's (may Allah be pleased with her) husband was a slave."
"1268","It is narrated from Ibn Sirin, may Allah have mercy on him, that he said: ""The one who holds the contract of marriage in his hand is the husband."""
"1269","Saeed bin Jubair (may Allah have mercy on him) said that the one who holds the contract of marriage in his hand is the husband."
"1270","It is narrated from Ibn Jurayj (may Allah have mercy on him) that he received this information from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that he said: ""He is the husband."""
"1271","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: ""For her, the dowry is half, and there is absolutely no waiting period (‘iddah) for her, meaning the woman about whom Allah Almighty has said: 'And if you divorce women before you have touched them and you have already specified a dowry for them...' (__QUR_2:237__) and Allah Almighty's statement: 'Then if you divorce them before you have touched them, there is no waiting period for you to count against them...' (__QUR_33:49__).”"
"1272","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he used to say: ""Every divorced woman is entitled to mut‘ah (a parting gift) except for the woman whose dowry has been fixed and then she is divorced before consummation; in that case, half of her dowry will be counted for her."""
"1273","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he used to say: Every divorced woman is entitled to maintenance upon divorce, except for the one whose dowry has been specified and then she is divorced before consummation; for her, only the specified dowry will be counted."
"1274","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said regarding the man who, after marriage, was alone with his wife but did not have intercourse, and then divorced her, that half of the dowry is obligatory upon him, because Allah Almighty says: ""And if you divorce them before you have touched them, and you have appointed for them a dowry, then give half of what you appointed"" (Al-Baqarah: 237)."
"1275","Muhammad bin Jubair bin Mut’im narrated from his father that he married a woman and divorced her before having intercourse with her, then he sent her the full dowry. When he was asked about this matter, he said: “I have more right to dispose of the remaining property.”"
"1276","Humaid bin Abdur Rahman bin Awf, Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, and Sulaiman bin Yasar narrate that they heard Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I asked Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) about the man from the people of Bahrain who gave his wife one or two divorces, then her waiting period ended, and then another man married her, then he also divorced her or he died, then her first husband married her again. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Now this husband will have the right to the remaining (divorces)."""
